{
  "_specimen": "FIRST PHYSICAL .qm SPECIMEN. Not a format, not a schema, not a language, not executable, not a replacement for main.py. The physical extension `.qm` is the thing under test; the bytes inside are JSON purely because that was convenient today. Every field name here is EXPERIMENTAL and unjustified — no other file may be written against it.",
  "_derived_from": "knowledge/quantum/main.quantum.json, fourth edition. Only what this linking experiment needs was carried over; the audit prose was deliberately left behind.",
  "_experiment": "Can a .qm artifact physically exist, carry a proven semantic object, and participate in a cross-file relationship that a machine can resolve and falsify? Validator: scripts/qm_link_check.py (experimental, outside the production runtime).",
  "subject": {
    "path": "main.py",
    "commit": "6880462",
    "sha256_prefix": "def397b4c33e51d3",
    "_subject_identity_is_open": "OPEN FUNDAMENTAL, carried over unresolved. This specimen is NAMED after main.py, but the audit proved its claims are owned by five files. Probe QT1 falsified a claim by editing cli/app.py while main.py stayed byte-identical. The `subject` block below is therefore an ADDRESS, not a proof of ownership, and this specimen deliberately links only an entity whose evidence lives outside main.py — so the experiment does not hide the defect behind a convenient choice."
  },
  "entry": {
    "_status": "EXPERIMENTAL ADDITION, experiment 2 of the entry-point replacement test. Experiment 1 measured that the specimen carried NO producer-side fact and therefore no launcher could construct an invocation from it. This block is the minimum that closes that gap and nothing more.",
    "_derivation": "NOT invented. The fourth-edition record already proved both facts: main.py's body is `return run_cli()` with run_cli imported from cli.app, and its module tail is `raise SystemExit(main())`. Those two facts are carried here. No new semantics were designed to make this experiment succeed.",
    "_what_is_deliberately_absent": "no flags, no defaults, no mode selection, no environment. All of that lives in cli/app.py and stays there — this experiment replaces the ENTRY ARTIFACT, not the implementation.",
    "delegate": {
      "module": "cli.app",
      "callable": "run_cli"
    },
    "termination": "raise SystemExit(<the delegate's return value>)",
    "argv0": "main.qm",
    "_argv0_note": "the entry artifact names itself. argparse derives `prog` from argv[0], so the usage line will read `main.qm` and NOT `main.py`. That difference is left visible on purpose: faking argv[0] back to main.py would be reconstructing the identity of the file this experiment removed.",
    "forbidden_in_the_launch_path": [
      "main.py"
    ],
    "_forbidden_note": "machine-enforced by an audit hook in the launcher, not merely asserted."
  },
  "semantic_entities": {
